    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 45 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires the owner response to include `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` integer property (0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the code generator produces the field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` that calls a new `luhn(...)` helper. The helper walks the `customerCode` right-to-left, skips non-digit separators (e.g. the `-` in `SYD-SMI-0007`), doubles every second digit starting from the rightmost, and returns `(10 - sum % 10) % 10` \u2014 matching the exact algorithm the test recomputes.\n\nThe value flows through the existing pipeline: `AssignCustomerCode` sets the code, and `RespondWithOwner`/`ListOwners` map the entity to `OwnerDto`, now including the derived `checkDigit`. `Cp31Tests` and the full suite (45 tests) are green.",
